  "policy": {
    "anchor": "Keep every original S640 supported10 detection and origin in exact input order, without coordinate/class/confidence replacement.",
    "proposals": "Use complete S640 detail-supported12 results from the same source image, with their original origins. These already obey the unchanged two-view support rule. No class-specific filtering or new threshold.",
    "anchor_veto": "Reject any proposal overlapping any anchor at f32 IoU>.45, regardless of class.",
    "addition_nms": "Sort proposals by confidence descending, class, left and input rank; classwise f32 IoU>.45 NMS only between accepted additions. Append to anchor, total<=300.",
    "limits": "Source image positive dimensions <=16M pixels, each input list<=300 finite valid boxes, confidence in[.3,1], origins view<16/rank<300 with unique origins per input. <=180000 IoU comparisons. Complete JSON input/output<=4MiB; no clobber.",
    "interpretation": "Explicit model-free measured-box postprocessing, not proof of model execution or admission of external inference reports. The evaluator separately verifies full original native parents and their common four-view prefix. Retaining predictions does not mathematically guarantee greedy ground-truth match retention."
  },
  "evaluation": "Viewed40: reuse first/repeat/original S640 supported10 and detail-supported12 parents,240 reports and2640 old forwards, never recounted. Fresh16: run each frozen producer twice optimized and once original graph:16*(10+12)*3=1056 new forwards. Postprocess all56 pairs in Rust on each of three passes:168 fixture runs, zero model forwards. Score same complete labels in coarse4, supported10, detail-supported12 and preserved union.",
  "relative_adoption": "In both viewed40 and fresh16, preserved precision must not regress versus coarse4 or supported10, recall must exceed both, and every present-class recall must not regress versus either supported baseline. Every original supported10 matched reference must also be retained. Fresh16 must pass all unchanged absolute gates. Otherwise no default adoption."
